  "notes": {
    "multi-module-correctness": "The plan puts multi-module-correctness in L1 and its source parts in L5. Only the .prod file is black-box; the main file imports createCrossModuleFactsProxy and is white-box (see WHITE-BOX.md), so its split waits for that triage.",
    "effects": "The plan's ladder puts basic effects (run, cleanup, auto-tracking) at L0 and full effects (deps/on, prev, per-frame skip-tracking) at L4. So the black-box effects files' rule is L0 (read-only views, L1, for blackbox-effects-readonly) and each test that uses deps, on or prev is lifted to L4 by those options (lib/layers.ts OPTION_LAYERS). The plan's L4 files effects and effects-lazy-prev-facts are white-box (derivationDep, declaresPrevFacts).",
    "predicate": "predicate and predicate-describe (L11) and sweep-under are white-box.",
    "derive data forms": "A derivation whose compute is a predicate ({ $gte: … }) or a $template is evaluated by the predicate DSL, which the plan's ladder puts at L11 (Predicates DSL). lib/layers.ts used to place this signal at L1, so mutants-derivations' 'freezes a predicate spec and a template spec at registration' ran at L1 and failed an L1 engine that had no predicates to evaluate. The signal now places at L11. The plan's L1 'data-forms' entry is the data-forms files (when/on data forms on modules), which this signal never placed.",
    "per-test placement": "A file's rule is now a default, not a floor: a test is placed by the features found in its own body, its describes' hooks and declarations and the file-level code it reaches (lib/layers.ts reachable). Only a test that builds a system and shows nothing beyond the vehicle (createSystem, createModule) and the schema builders (t) takes its file's rule. The L0 reads, writes and definitions (facts, derive, events, dispatch, read, subscribe, watch, batch; init/derive/events/effects options) count as found but never raise a test; module hooks, initialFacts and tickMs are L3 signals (lifecycle, ssr, clock). So engine.test's 'facts proxy reads and writes values' sits at L0, while 'system.start() sets isRunning true' (no feature beyond the vehicle) stays at the file's L3."
  },
  "instrumentNotes": {
    "option plugins": "observes resolver outcomes through plugin hooks (onResolverComplete/Cancel/Error); L2 must expose them",
    "member .inspect": "reads requirement state through system.inspect(); L2 must expose it",
    "import flushMicrotasks": "a one-line microtask flush from /testing; L2 tests need it before the testing subpath (L13) exists"
  }
